foundation.question_text:
The diagram shows the curve $y = f(x)$. Over which values of $x$ is the curve concave down?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[axis lines=middle, xlabel={$x$}, ylabel={$y$},
             xmin=-2.5, xmax=7.4, ymin=-6.7, ymax=6.0, samples=100, clip=false,
             xtick={-2,-1,1,2,3,4,5,6,7}, ytick={-6,-4,-2,2,4}]
\addplot[smooth, thick, <->, domain=-1.96:6.62] {0.2*(x*x*x - 6*x*x)};
\node[font=\small] at (axis cs:1.3,3.4) {$y=f(x)$};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

development.solution_text:
$\dfrac{dy}{dx} = 4x^{3} - 12x$
$\dfrac{d^{2}y}{dx^{2}} = 12x^{2} - 12$
For concave down, $\dfrac{d^{2}y}{dx^{2}} < 0$:
$12x^{2} - 12 < 0$
$x^{2} < 1$
$-1 < x < 1$
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[axis lines=middle, xlabel={$x$}, ylabel={$y$},
             xmin=-2.9, xmax=2.9, ymin=-3.5, ymax=11.5, samples=100, clip=false,
             xtick={-2,-1,1,2}, ytick={2,4,6,8,10}]
\addplot[smooth, thick, <->, domain=-2.58:2.58] {x*x*x*x - 6*x*x + 7};
\draw[dashed] (axis cs:-1,-3.5) -- (axis cs:-1,11.5);
\draw[dashed] (axis cs:1,-3.5) -- (axis cs:1,11.5);
\node[font=\small] at (axis cs:0,-2.4) {concave down};
\node[font=\small] at (axis cs:2.1,8.6) {$y=f(x)$};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
